			"width": 600,
			"height": 851,
			"color": "4",
			"label": "What each ESM score means"
		},
		{
			"id": "m-src",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Raw · MiEYE\n- light logger worn at eye level\n- per-epoch spectral channels (melanopic, rhodopic, photopic, cones) + motion + charger\n- an Excel sheet saved with a `.csv` name — only that sheet is read",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 1900,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 220
		},
		{
			"id": "a-s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Step 1 · Epoching\n**In:** raw `.bin`   **Out:** one row per **60 s** → `_60s.csv`\n\n- **SVM** — how much movement in that minute, with gravity taken out\n  `SVM = Σ over the minute of | length of the 3-axis vector − 1 g |`\n  *a perfectly still device reads ≈ 0*\n- **axis means** — which way the device was facing\n- **axis SDs** — how much it shook (used later to spot non-wear)",
			"x": 580,
			"y": 110,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 320,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-src",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Raw · Actigraph\n- GENEActiv `.bin`, worn on the wrist\n- 3 axes sampled at **100 Hz** (~8.6 M readings a day)\n- ~1.1 GB, usually a cloud placeholder → downloaded first\n- one recording per participant-season",
			"x": -20,
			"y": 160,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 220
		},
		{
			"id": "a-m10",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### M10 · L5 — when the day peaks and rests\n- **M10** = mean activity over the **most active 10 hours**\n- **L5** = mean activity over the **least active 5 hours**\n- each gives a **level** (how much) and an **onset hour** (when it starts)\n- measured noon → noon, so a night is never split across two days\n\n`M10 = highest 10-hour rolling mean of hourly activity`\n`L5  = lowest 5-hour rolling mean of hourly activity`",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": -6,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 303,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-isiv",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### IS · IV — how regular, how broken\n- **IS** (interdaily stability) — do the days look alike? **0 = random, 1 = identical days**\n  `IS = variance of the average 24-hour day ÷ variance of all hours`\n- **IV** (intradaily variability) — how much it jumps hour to hour; **higher = more fragmented**\n  `IV = mean squared change between neighbouring hours ÷ variance of all hours`",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 270,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-ra",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### RA — strength of the rhythm\n- the contrast between the active and the resting part of the day, on a 0–1 scale\n- **higher = a sharper day/night difference**\n\n`RA = (M10 − L5) ÷ (M10 + L5)`",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 600,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 190,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-per",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Periodogram — is there a ~24 h cycle at all?\n- tries every period from **14 h to 34 h** and reports which fits best\n- a healthy rhythm peaks at ≈ 24 h\n\n`strength(P) = variance explained by folding the data at period P ÷ total variance`",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 1160,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 210,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-out",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Step 2 · what it writes\n**In:** `_60s.csv`   **Out:** per recording\n\n- `_60s_nonparametric.csv` — IS, IV, M10, L5 (one row)\n- `_60s_daily.csv` — M10 / L5 **for each day**\n- `_60s_sri.csv` — SRI + how many days it used\n- `_60s_periodogram.csv` — period vs strength\n- `_60s_report.pdf` — the plots a reviewer actually looks at",
			"x": 1920,
			"y": 330,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 320,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-comp",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Compliance · was it worn?\n**In:** the 60-s epochs   **Out:** one verdict\n\n- **non-wear** — 2 of 3 axis SDs below **13 mg** for **≥ 30 min** *(a worn wrist always twitches)*\n- **valid day** — ≥ **10 h** wear **and** an hourly activity range ≥ 20 *(a real day/night swing)*\n- **verdict** — **PASS** ≥ 3 valid days · **REVIEW** within 1 · else **FAIL**\n- writes `_compliance.json` · `_daily_compliance.csv` · `.xlsx`",
			"x": 2560,
			"y": 330,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 340,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "a-sri",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### SRI — same time of day, same state?\n- every minute is scored **sleep or wake** (Cole–Kripke 1992, step 2's published constants)\n- then: at the same clock minute on the next day, was it the same state?\n\n`SRI = 2 × (% of day-to-day minute pairs that match) − 100`\n\n- **100 = perfectly repeating · 0 = coin toss**\n- the sleep/wake call uses a fixed cut-off, so it is sensitive to any rescaling of activity",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 809,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 330,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "m-comp",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Compliance · worn, in daylight?\n- the device is **charged regularly, so charging ≠ wearing**\n- the test is the **shape of the day**:\n  - day:night melanopic ratio **≥ 2**\n  - **and** ≥ 10 h above the light floor\n- **verdict** — PASS ≥ 3 valid days · REVIEW within 1 · else FAIL",
			"x": 2560,
			"y": 1880,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 280,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "master",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# Master · the churned data\n`…\\CDxxx\\<Season>\\<Device>\\`\n\n**Collated per participant × season × device**\n\n- every device writes a `_compliance.json` **in the same shape** → one verdict table across devices\n- the day-level CSVs sit beside it, so values can be re-read **without re-running anything**\n- the season folder also holds the assessment log\n- per participant: `CDxxx_compliance_summary.csv/.xlsx`",
			"x": 3240,
			"y": 1700,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 460,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "t-saliva",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Saliva\n- cortisol / melatonin assays\n- format and timing not decided yet",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 4110,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "t-batch",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Cognitron · Qualtrics\n- exported **batched by upload date**, not per participant → a **collate** step is needed first\n- Cognitron also needs a `user_id` ↔ E-code crosswalk, which does not exist yet",
			"x": 640,
			"y": 4110,
			"width": 1160,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "t-none",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## No verdict\n- nothing rolls up for these yet",
			"x": 2560,
			"y": 4110,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "m-s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Light processing\n**In:** the logged sheet   **Out:** per-day metrics + report\n\n- works in **melanopic EDI** — the part of light the body clock responds to\n- kept on a **log scale**: indoors ≈ 100 lx, daylight ≈ 100 000 lx",
			"x": 561,
			"y": 1882,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 260,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "m-out",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## What it writes\n- `_luminosity_metrics.csv` — per-day light metrics\n- `_light_windows.csv` — M5 / M7 / L2 per day\n- `_hourly_dark_histogram.csv`\n- `_luminosity_report.pdf` — heatmaps, zones, daily dose\n- `_compliance.json` · `_daily_compliance.csv`",
			"x": 1995,
			"y": 1880,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 280,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "doc",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Season paperwork\n- the **assessment log** from staging, copied as-is\n- says what was *meant* to happen: visit number, device start dates, agreed bed/wake times\n- maps **Day 1–15 of ESM to real dates**",
			"x": 3173,
			"y": 2401,
			"width": 700,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "d-vis",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ② Visualise (tab)\n**In:** every `_compliance.json`   **Out:** nothing — a reader\n\n- grid coloured by verdict, per participant\n- aggregate: passed / review / failed and mean % compliance, by device and season\n- drill into one recording: its daily table and report PDF",
			"x": 4360,
			"y": 940,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 320,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "d-run",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ① Compliance (tab)\n**In:** staging   **Out:** the master tree\n\n- **⚑ naming check first** — a filename that drifts gets skipped or mis-attributed\n- **RUN**: new & unfinished · preview · force\n- **initials required** for anything that writes\n- live progress per step, cancellable",
			"x": 4360,
			"y": 420,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 320,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "d-t2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ③ T2 (tab) — reads only\n**In:** the day-level CSVs for the chosen participants, seasons and devices\n\n- devices lined up on **real dates**; a night is keyed to the **evening it starts**\n- **Coverage** — which days exist, and the window where all chosen devices overlap\n- **Agreement** — two measures in the same unit, day by day *(clock hours wrap: 23:00 vs 01:00 is 2 h apart, not 22)*\n- **Relationships** — within one person's own days vs between different people\n- **Compare** — by season of the year, by group, or by person\n\n**Out:** nothing until Export",
			"x": 4360,
			"y": 1540,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 480,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "recompute",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Recompute *(planned · experimental)*\n**In:** a T2 cohort **you already created**\n**Out:** an extra epoch file in master **+ a derived cohort**\n\n- **step 1 only**, at a different epoch (e.g. 30 s)\n- writes `variant.json` + `<stem>_30s.csv` into `_variants/`\n- step 2 is a **separate press**, afterwards\n- **compliance is never re-run** — the 60 s verdict stands\n- the derived cohort is a **subset of its parent — never larger** — and records which cohort it came from",
			"x": 4400,
			"y": 2200,
			"width": 480,
			"height": 380,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "runs",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## runs/ — the record of what was done\n- **batches/** — public, stripped: who, when, mode, counts, thresholds, tool versions\n- **_private/** — participants and per-item results, stays on the machine",
			"x": 5200,
			"y": 940,
			"width": 480,
			"height": 320,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "m-when",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### When the light falls\n- **M5 / M7** — the **brightest** 5 h and 7 h: onset hour + level\n- **L2** — the **darkest** 2 h: onset hour + level\n- these are the hours compared against the Actigraph rest window, to see whether light and sleep line up",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 1970,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 240,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "m-dose",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Dose over the study\n- **daily dose** — total melanopic exposure per day\n- **time in zones** — how long spent dark / dim / bright\n- **hourly dark histogram** — which hours of the day were dark",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 2260,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 220,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "m-amount",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### How much light\n- **day mean / night mean** — average melanopic EDI inside 07–19 and 23–06\n- **TAT 250** — minutes at or above **250 lx** during the day *(the daytime target)*\n- **TBT 10** — minutes below **10 lx** at night *(the darkness target)*\n- **geometric mean** — the average of log₁₀(light), because the scale spans 5 orders of magnitude",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 1660,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 260,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "x-adh",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Adherence\n- **response rate** — how much of the protocol was actually answered\n\n`response rate = completed prompts ÷ expected prompts`\n\n- also: median delay before answering, and % answered inside the prompt window",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 2700,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 230,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "x-diary",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Sleep diary — the reported night\n- **TST** total sleep time · **SOL** time to fall asleep · **WASO** awake during the night · **SE** sleep efficiency\n\n`TST = (lights out → final wake) − SOL − WASO`\n`SE  = TST ÷ time in bed`\n\n- filled in the morning, so it describes **the night before**",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 2970,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 270,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "x-affect",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Affect — mood in the moment\n- **positive / negative affect** — the mean of the pleasant and the unpleasant items (1–7)\n- several responses a day, each with its own timestamp",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 3280,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 190,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "x-comp",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Compliance · enough answers?\n- pooled response rate across the **scored** surveys\n- **PASS** ≥ 70 % · **REVIEW** within 10 points · else **FAIL**",
			"x": 2560,
			"y": 2950,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "x-out",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## What it writes\n- `_expiwell_metrics.csv` — response rate per survey\n- `_expiwell_sleep_metrics.csv` — one row per night\n- `_expiwell_affect.csv` — one row per response\n- `_expiwell_item_series.csv` / `_item_measures.csv` — item level\n- `_expiwell_report.pdf` · `_compliance.json`",
			"x": 1925,
			"y": 2945,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 280,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "x-src",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Raw · Expiwell\n- one CSV per survey: Affect, Sleep-Diary, Cognitron prompt, …\n- 4 header rows before the data starts\n- **only completed responses are exported** — misses are invisible in the file",
			"x": -37,
			"y": 2696,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 220
		},
		{
			"id": "x-s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Schedule + scoring\n**In:** survey CSVs   **Out:** per-response and per-night values\n\n- the **expected** number of prompts has to be configured — the file cannot say what was missed\n- every response keeps its **real timestamp**: day-of-study is not a calendar count",
			"x": 636,
			"y": 2682,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 280,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "sharepoint",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# Raw data · SharePoint / OneDrive\n`Tier 1\\staging\\CDxxx\\<Season>\\<Device>\\`\n\n- uploaded by the research team: **one folder per participant, per season**\n- **read-only** — the pipeline never writes back here\n- everything to the right turns this into numbers other people can analyse",
			"x": -1067,
			"y": 1906,
			"width": 637,
			"height": 220,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "d-exp",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ④ Export — Tier 2 Research Cohorts\n- lists every file **before** writing, then takes the **approver's initials**\n\n**Out:** `<t2_root>\\T2-<date>-<initials>-<seasons>\\`\n- tidy data + one row per participant-day\n- dictionary of every measure\n- charts PDF + the device report PDFs\n- **manifest** — thresholds used, tool versions, SHA-256 of every input file",
			"x": 5164,
			"y": 1622,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 305,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2out",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 6050,
			"y": 1640,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 280,
			"color": "4",
			"text": "# Tier 2 · the delivered dataset\n**`<t2_root>`** — a different place from master\n\n- one folder per export, written once, **never edited**\n- re-exporting makes a **new** folder\n- participant IDs are pseudonymised **here and only here**\n- carries its own `manifest.json`: inputs, thresholds, tool versions"
		}
